  <Docs>
    <summary>Selects whether a KeyChain lookup uses device-wide keys or keys for the current user.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>This .NET enum maps the <c>KEYPAIR_SCOPE_*</c> constants accepted by <see cref="T:Android.Security.KeyChainManager" />. Device scope includes keys visible to affiliated users; user scope limits the lookup to the current user's credentials. Select one scope for each lookup.</para>
      <para>See the <see href="https://github.com/dotnet/android/blob/a816eb807a0468d53a23ab45cfdffe9f8badfd6c/src/Mono.Android/map.csv#L13543-L13544">binding enum mappings</see> and the <see href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/security/KeyChainManager#KEYPAIR_SCOPE_DEVICE">Android scope definitions</see>.</para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
